                    <chunk name="param_input" index="4">
                      <items count="9">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Where the LiDAR comes from. Auto: AHN inside the Netherlands, swissSURFACE3D, Bavaria, IGN LiDAR HD, Scotland's National LiDAR Programme, Estonia, Denmark, Slovenia, Saxony, Luxembourg, Brussels, Navarra or Spain's PNOA where the site lies in one, else USGS 3DEP (its newest project over the site). Browse… picks one dataset: "3DEP &lt;project&gt;" reads that project, "AHN &lt;sheet&gt;" reads AHN. NOAA Digital Coast is asked for by name, never by Auto: county and city surveys on the US coasts and the Great Lakes, often newer and denser than 3DEP and with a building class ("NOAA &lt;id&gt;" reads one dataset). Or type an http(s) URL of any LAS/LAZ file (metric coordinates): it is downloaded once into the cache and cropped around Cloud Centre. Or the full path of a LAS/LAZ (or x y z [class] text) file on this machine — your own survey: it is read in place and cropped the same way; press Re-run after replacing the file.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">fa86ada8-eec3-4f99-92e8-bba48f0cef5b</item>
                        <item name="Multiple" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
