                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Also fetch OpenStreetMap roads, paved surfaces and footpaths (highway centrelines buffered by their width or lane count, area:highway, car parks, paved plazas; footways and sidewalks, paths, cycleways and steps, 1.5-2.5 m where untagged) as three more Layer Outlines layers, 'roads', 'paved' and 'paths', that City Surface carries as their own triangle groups following the terrain. A path loses the ground a road or a paved area holds. Also one more query for the street's own objects — fences, walls and hedges (Barriers), benches, bus stops, hydrants and picnic tables (Furniture) — as simple solids on the ground.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">c49dc326-7f78-4e12-90e5-57c1fc0fad24</item>
